selected fences preserve order, scope and source locations: true
shared groups preserve source order: true
different documents have independent scopes even for the same group name: true
coverage counts every selected block rather than deduplicating groups: true
horizontal whitespace in fence metadata keeps the annotation active: true
an annotation on an unsupported language fails loudly: true
agent-note code spans are extracted: true
historical and unselected blocks stay outside compilation: true
non-OCaml fences do not expose nested fake annotations: true
an empty compilation selection is refused: true
malformed annotations fail loudly: true
unsupported annotated indentation and unclosed fences fail loudly: true
malformed inline selection cannot silently disappear: true
an excerpt matching its source up to whitespace is accepted: true
the drifted capture slide, reintroduced under its annotation, is refused at its first drifted line: true
the drifted examples slide is refused without a provenance declaration: true
the drifted examples slide is refused as an excerpt: true
an adaptation naming no file is refused: true
an adaptation naming an existing file is accepted: true
an empty excerpt is refused: true
a caption citing an OCaml source directly above a fence requires a declaration: true
a caption apart from the fence, or citing another language, requires none: true
a provenance declaration is read on any fence language, next to the language word only: true
a quoted fence is read through its quote markers, and checked when annotated: true
a quoted annotated fence the quote abandons, or a nested quote, fails loudly: true
